    {
      "name": "subscribing after a snapshot does not double the session",
      "why": "The load-bearing case. events.subscribe replays the current session as synthetic creation events, so a client that snapshots and then subscribes is told every existing entity was just created - 7 events for a one-pane session in the recording, 9 for a three-pane one. Convergence is what makes that harmless, and it is a property of the vocabulary rather than a rule each adapter remembers: there is no 'created' event to get wrong, only an upsert.",
