      "why": "herdr says pane_exited for a program that ended and pane_closed for a pane a client closed, and never both - the recorded stream goes straight from pane_exited to layout_updated. Muster keeps no such distinction, because both mean the surface should stop existing and keeping the difference would invite handling only one of them. This case pins that one vocabulary word covers both, so the adapter has nowhere to put half the behavior.",
