    {
      "name": "a replayed pane does not roll back a live agent state",
      "why": "herdr replays the session as it stood when the subscription opened, and its pane payloads carry agent_status. Letting a structure event write that field makes the backend two writers for it, the replay being the older one, and nothing arrives afterwards to correct the rollback - agent state comes on its own per-pane subscription. A pane stuck showing idle while its agent works is this product failing at the one thing it is for.\n\nThe relabel beside it is incidental to that and is still correct: the replayed payload carries a directory the snapshot did not, and what a pane is called is a thing structure events are allowed to write. Only the agent's state is fenced off.",
      "given": {
        "snapshot": {
          "panes": [
            {
              "id": "w1:p1",
              "tab": "w1:t1",
              "workspace": "w1",
              "agentState": "idle"
