        "panes": [
          "w1:p1"
        ],
        "tabs": [],
        "workspaces": [],
        "agentStates": {
          "w1:p1": "working"
        },
        "layouts": {},
        "focus": {},
        "health": "connected",
        "changes": [
          "agentStateChanged:w1:p1:idle->working",
          "paneRelabelled:w1:p1"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "detecting a harness renames the pane, and moves nothing else",
      "why": "herdr identifies a harness by reading the screen, seconds after the pane started, so a pane is listed before anything knows what is running in it. A list that names panes by their directory and harness would say `src` forever unless this is reported - and on a quiet session nothing else ever comes along to correct it. Reported as a rename rather than as a state change, because an agent that has just been recognized was already doing whatever it was doing.",
