    {
      "name": "transitions that ran while nobody was listening are reported on reconnect",
      "why": "herdr stamps agent transitions from one session-wide counter, and that stamp reaches a client in exactly one place: the agents[] of a snapshot. It is never on an event. So a gap is visible only by comparing two snapshots against the transitions applied in between - here one was applied and the counter moved by four. Muster exists to route attention, so an agent that asked for the user during the gap has to be surfaced rather than quietly overwritten by the fresh snapshot.",
